UX pattern implemented for delete_edge error handling:

BEFORE (typical approach):
  Error: Edge from 5 to 99 does not exist.

AFTER (helpful approach):
  Error: No edge from node 5 to node 99. Node 5 has edges to: 12, 15, 18

Why this matters:
1. User doesn't have to run separate command to find valid targets
2. Reduces frustration when making typos in node IDs
3. Guides user toward correct action immediately
4. Follows existing pattern in create_edge validation

Implementation:
```rust
let outgoing: Vec<DecisionEdge> = decision_edges::table
    .filter(decision_edges::from_node_id.eq(from_id))
    .load(&mut conn)?;

if outgoing.is_empty() {
    return Err(DbError::Validation(format!(
        "No edge from node {} to node {}. Node {} has no outgoing edges.",
        from_id, to_id, from_id
    )));
} else {
    let targets: Vec<String> = outgoing.iter()
        .map(|e| e.to_node_id.to_string()).collect();
    return Err(DbError::Validation(format!(
        "No edge from node {} to node {}. Node {} has edges to: {}",
        from_id, to_id, from_id, targets.join(", ")
    )));
}
```

Added command variants to src/main.rs Command enum (lines 93-110):

Location: After Link command, before Status command
Pattern: Follows existing command structure with clap derive macros

Code added:
```rust
/// Remove an edge between two nodes
Unlink {
    /// Source node ID
    from: i32,

    /// Target node ID
    to: i32,
},

/// Delete a node and all its connected edges
Delete {
    /// Node ID to delete
    id: i32,

    /// Show what would be deleted without actually deleting
    #[arg(long)]
    dry_run: bool,
},
```

Design decisions in this code:
- Unlink mirrors Link's from/to signature (not edge ID) for consistency
- Delete takes single node ID (matches show, status commands)
- dry_run is --dry-run flag (long only, no short) to prevent accidental use
- Doc comments become help text automatically via clap derive

Added command handlers to src/main.rs match statement (lines 628-660):

Location: After Link handler, before Status handler
Pattern: Follows existing error handling with colored output

Unlink handler (lines 628-634):
```rust
Command::Unlink { from, to } => match db.delete_edge(from, to) {
    Ok(()) => println!("{} edge ({} -> {})", "Removed".red(), from, to),
    Err(e) => {
        eprintln!("{} {}", "Error:".red(), e);
        std::process::exit(1);
    }
},
```

Delete handler (lines 636-660):
```rust
Command::Delete { id, dry_run } => match db.delete_node(id, dry_run) {
    Ok(summary) => {
        if dry_run {
            println!(
                "{} Would delete node {} ({}) with {} edge(s)",
                "Dry run:".yellow(),
                id,
                summary.node_title,
                summary.edges_deleted
            );
        } else {
            println!(
                "{} node {} ({}) and {} edge(s)",
                "Deleted".red(),
                id,
                summary.node_title,
                summary.edges_deleted
            );
        }
    }
    Err(e) => {
        eprintln!("{} {}", "Error:".red(), e);
        std::process::exit(1);
    }
},
```

Output color choices:
- "Removed".red() / "Deleted".red() - destructive actions in red
- "Dry run:".yellow() - warning/preview in yellow
- Matches existing "Created".green() / "Updated".green() pattern
